    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (83.63) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) headline our lineup as the must-start anchors. **Corbin Carroll** thrives in a high-leverage spot against Junk, benefiting from a favorable 4.71 xERA matchup and a dynamic platoon advantage that boosts his overall efficiency profile. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** is positioned for a breakout performance; his score is buoyed significantly by a massive +14% park factor and an equally strong platoon edge against the opposing starter. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants attention with a 75.03 score, as his spot in the #2 hole against P\u00e9rez provides the most reliable opportunity for counting stats on the board today. \n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Austin Riley**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 50.87 score. While **Austin Riley** carries pedigree, his matchup against Gausman presents a daunting SP skill hurdle (-6%) and a poor BvP history, which ultimately tilted the optimizer toward the higher upside of **Josh Naylor** (73.48) and his excellent platoon-adjusted projection. Elsewhere, we are capitalizing on aggressive base-stealing opportunities; **Brice Turang** and **Jose Caballero** remain in the starting lineup specifically to exploit the slower deliveries of Bachar and Ober, respectively. While **Jose Caballero** faces a steep -13% penalty due to platoon dynamics, his elite speed and the \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus keep him as a viable play for potential stolen bases.\n\nWe are monitoring the status of **James Wood**, who remains on the bench today due to an unfavorable matchup against S\u00e1nchez. Despite his elite 0.413 xwOBA, the combination of a tough pitcher and defensive metrics essentially forced a zero-score projection, mandating a stay on the bench to preserve our game caps. We are also wary of the risk surrounding **Zach McKinstry**; his score of 46.84 is precariously close to our \"Below floor\" threshold, largely driven by a -6% penalty for hitting in the #8 spot. As always, we are keeping a close watch on **Moises Ballesteros**, who needs to overcome a tough test against Gilbert to maintain value in the #5 spot.",
